{"file":"Mind++ for Claude-1.2.5-v2.zip","bytes":235455,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"mind-plus-plus","description":"Your second brain powered by Claude — captures meetings, tracks commitments, delivers daily briefs, and maintains a living knowledge base for your professional and personal life.","version":"1.2.5","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/felipe-venturini/mind-plus-plus","homepage":"https://github.com/felipe-venturini/mind-plus-plus","keywords":["obsidian","pkm","second-brain","knowledge-management","productivity","meetings","tasks","zettelkasten"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/capture-idea/SKILL.md","name":"capture-idea","description":"Captures a quick idea, note, or thought with minimum friction — auto-classifies the context (client, product, personal, operational) and saves it to the right place, or routes to inbox/ when uncertain. Use when the user says 'note this', 'quick note', 'idea:', 'capture this', 'jot down', 'save this thought', or shares a standalone thought without framing it as a task or meeting.","headings":["Skill: capture-idea","What this skill does","Step 1 — Extract the raw content","Step 2 — Classify the context","Step 3 — Decide the destination file","Step 4 — Write the file","Step 5 — Confirm in chat","Edge cases"],"name_hint":"capture · idea","description_zh":"快速捕获独立想法、笔记或思考，自动识别客户、产品、个人或运营背景并保存到合适位置，无法判断时放入inbox。"},{"path":"skills/daily-brief/SKILL.md","name":"daily-brief","description":"Generates the morning situational briefing — today's agenda, urgent tasks, overdue follow-ups, and contexts without recent contact. Use ALWAYS when the user says 'brief', 'what do I have today', 'daily summary', 'what's overdue', 'catch me up', 'morning update', or opens the system in the morning without a specific request. Scans all task files in the vault, cross-references the day's calendar, and delivers a situation panel in under 2 minutes of reading.","headings":["Skill: daily-brief","What this skill delivers","Step 1 — Today's agenda","Step 2 — Scan tasks","Step 3 — Check last touchpoint","Step 4 — Compose the brief","Brief — {weekday}, {YYYY-MM-DD}","🗓️ Today's agenda","🔴 Urgent — overdue or due today","🟡 Chase others","🟢 No recent contact (>14 days)","📅 Next 3 business days","Step 5 — Save (optional)","Notes"],"name_hint":"daily · brief","description_zh":"扫描知识库任务并对照当日日历，生成晨间简报，包含议程、紧急任务、逾期跟进及久未联系的背景，按原说明控制在两分钟阅读量。"},{"path":"skills/knowledge-search/SKILL.md","name":"knowledge-search","description":"Searches the vault by topic or question and returns a synthesized answer with wikilinks to the source notes. Use when the user says 'what do I know about X', 'everything we discussed about Y', 'find notes on Z', 'what did we decide about...', 'search the vault for...', or asks any question that should be answered from the user's own accumulated knowledge rather than general reasoning.","headings":["Skill: knowledge-search","What this skill does","Step 1 — Parse the query","Step 2 — Scope the search","Step 3 — Execute the search","Step 4 — Synthesize","📌 Short answer","📖 Context","🕰️ Timeline (only if relevant)","⚠️ Open threads","🔗 All sources","Step 5 — Be honest about gaps","Edge cases"],"name_hint":"知识 · 搜索","description_zh":"按主题问题搜索个人知识库，综合回答并用wikilink关联来源笔记，支持先前讨论、决策与积累知识查询。"},{"path":"skills/meeting-prep/SKILL.md","name":"meeting-prep","description":"Prepares a briefing for an upcoming meeting by pulling recent meetings, open tasks, pending decisions, and unresolved follow-ups for the relevant client, product, or person. Use when the user says 'prep for meeting with X', 'what should I talk about with X', 'brief me on X before the call', 'what's pending with X', or mentions a meeting that is about to happen.","headings":["Skill: meeting-prep","What this skill does","Step 1 — Identify the context","Step 2 — Gather signals","Step 3 — Produce the briefing","📋 Context","🎯 Likely agenda","⚠️ You owe them","🔄 They owe you","❓ Open questions","💡 Suggested talking points","🔗 Recent artifacts","Step 4 — Offer next steps","Edge cases"],"name_hint":"会议 · prep","description_zh":"为即将举行的会议汇总相关客户、产品或人员近期会议、未结任务、待决事项与未完成跟进，形成会前简报。"},{"path":"skills/new-decision/SKILL.md","name":"new-decision","description":"Records an architecture or business decision as a structured ADR (Architecture Decision Record) with context, decision, consequences, and rejected alternatives. Use when the user says 'record a decision', 'new ADR', 'document this decision', 'we decided X', 'create a decision doc', or describes a choice that deserves to be memorialized.","headings":["Skill: new-decision","What this skill does","Step 1 — Identify the decision and its scope","Step 2 — Determine the ADR number","Step 3 — Gather the supporting context","Step 4 — Write the ADR","ADR-{NNN}: {Title}","Status","Context","Decision","Consequences","Positive","Negative","Neutral","Alternatives considered","{Alternative 1}","{Alternative 2}","Stakeholders"],"name_hint":"new · decision","description_zh":"将架构或业务决策保存为结构化ADR，记录背景、决定、后果及被否决选项。"},{"path":"skills/new-meeting/SKILL.md","name":"new-meeting","description":"Processes a meeting and updates the vault. Use this skill whenever the user mentions a meeting, transcript, meeting notes, or automatic transcription email (Gemini, Fireflies, Otter). Trigger when the user says 'I had a meeting with X', 'process this transcript', 'save this meeting', 'log this call', or pastes raw notes. Every processed meeting results in a saved note + updated tasks + updated dashboard.","headings":["Skill: new-meeting","What this skill does","Step 1 — Identify the context","Step 2 — Read existing context","Step 3 — Create the meeting note","YYYY-MM-DD — Descriptive Title","Agenda","Notes","Decisions","Next steps","Step 4 — Update tasks","Step 5 — Update the dashboard","Step 6 — Confirm to the user"],"name_hint":"new · 会议","description_zh":"处理会议、转录、原始笔记及自动转录邮件，保存会议记录并同步任务和仪表板。"},{"path":"skills/process-inbox/SKILL.md","name":"process-inbox","description":"Triages the inbox/ folder — sorts files with no defined destination. Use this skill when the user says 'process inbox', 'what's in the inbox', 'organize inbox', 'triage files', 'clean inbox', or similar. Lists all files, identifies context via aliases and domain mapping, proposes a destination following vault conventions, and waits for confirmation before moving anything. Never moves files automatically.","headings":["Skill: process-inbox","What this skill does","Step 1 — List files in inbox","Step 2 — Identify each file","Step 3 — Present the proposal","Step 4 — Execute after confirmation","Step 5 — Confirm result"],"name_hint":"process · inbox","description_zh":"分流inbox中无目的地文件，依据别名、领域映射及知识库约定提出位置，确认后才移动；原说明明确不自动移动。"},{"path":"skills/process-meeting-emails/SKILL.md","name":"process-meeting-emails","description":"Automatic pipeline that ingests meeting transcription emails and creates structured notes in the vault. Use this skill when the user says 'process meeting emails', 'new meeting in email', 'run meeting pipeline', 'process transcripts', or when triggered by an automatic scheduled task. Searches for transcription emails (Gemini Meeting Notes, Fireflies, Otter, or similar), extracts meeting content, classifies contexts with ≥80% confidence, and generates formatted notes in the vault — no action is lost.","headings":["Skill: process-meeting-emails","What this skill does","Step 1 — Configuration check","Step 2 — Fetch emails","Step 3 — For each email found","Step 4 — Log the run","YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM","Step 5 — Phase 2 (only if authorized)"],"name_hint":"process · 会议 · emails","description_zh":"自动处理 Gemini Meeting Notes、Fireflies、Otter 等会议转录邮件，提取会议内容，以至少 80% 的置信度归入相应上下文，并在知识库中生成结构化纪要和行动项；支持手动触发或定时流程。"},{"path":"skills/setup-mind-plus-plus/SKILL.md","name":"setup-mind-plus-plus","description":"Sets up the Mind++ second brain from scratch — creates vault folder structure, captures the user profile, and generates configuration files. Use this skill when the user installs the plugin for the first time, says 'set up my second brain', 'set up mind plus plus', 'setup-mind-plus-plus', 'start from scratch', 'configure vault', or when no vault structure is found. Also trigger when the user wants to reset or update the base configuration of the system.","headings":["Skill: setup-mind-plus-plus","What this skill does","Step 1 — Detect current state","Step 2 — Capture user profile","Step 3 — Create folder structure","Base structure (always create)","Step 4 — Generate configuration files","`operational/config/domain-mapping.yml`","Email domain → client context mapping","Add your clients' email domains here","`operational/config/client-aliases.yml`","Keywords that identify each context in meeting titles and content","aliases:","acme: acme-corp","project-name: client-slug","`operational/tasks/Open Tasks.md`","Step 5 — Create or update CLAUDE.md","Step 6 — Offer scheduled tasks"],"name_hint":"设置 · mind · plus · plus","description_zh":"从零配置 Mind++ 第二大脑：创建知识库目录、采集用户档案并生成配置文件；用于首次安装、尚无知识库结构，以及重置或更新基础配置。"},{"path":"skills/specialist/SKILL.md","name":"specialist","description":"Routes a request to the right domain specialists and produces a vault-grounded deliverable. The domain is the first argument. Use when the user says '/specialist marketing ...', 'aciona um especialista de marketing', 'analisa a performance da campanha ...', 'qual o ROAS/ROI de ...', 'que números temos sobre ...', or asks for data analysis, media performance, data consistency, or a data-driven recommendation. Today the only domain is `marketing` (with the `bi` discipline).","headings":["Skill: specialist","What this skill does","Step 1 — Determine the domain","Step 2 — Parse the request","Step 3 — Load relevant vault history","Step 4 — Discover the domain's agents","Step 5 — Judge triage (which specialists to run)","Step 6 — Dispatch the selected specialists in parallel","Step 7 — Judge arbitration and resolution loop","Step 8 — Escalate open questions to the user (batched)","Step 9 — Present the reconciled answer","📌 Resposta","📄 Deliverable proposto","⚠️ Lacunas","Step 10 — Propose, confirm, write","Edge cases","Scaling note (for maintainers)"],"name_hint":"specialist","description_zh":"将请求交给相应领域专家，并依据知识库内容产出结果；原说明当前仅支持 marketing 领域及 bi 专业，用于营销活动表现、ROAS/ROI、数据一致性和数据驱动建议。"},{"path":"skills/stakeholder-update/SKILL.md","name":"stakeholder-update","description":"Generates a status update for a client, product, or project from vault content — recent meetings, decisions, open tasks, risks, and next steps. Use when the user says 'status update on X', 'client report for X', 'update for {stakeholder}', 'weekly status for the X project', 'prep a client-facing summary', or needs to communicate progress to someone external.","headings":["Skill: stakeholder-update","What this skill does","Step 1 — Identify the target and audience","Step 2 — Pull raw signals","Step 3 — Filter for external consumption","Step 4 — Draft the update","📅 {Context} — Status update, {date range}","✅ Progress since last update","🎯 Decisions made","🚧 In flight","⚠️ Risks & blockers","📌 Next steps","❓ Open questions for you","Step 5 — Adapt to channel","Step 6 — Offer before saving","Edge cases"],"name_hint":"stakeholder · 更新","description_zh":"依据知识库中的近期会议、决策、未完成任务、风险和下一步，生成客户、产品或项目的进展报告，便于向利益相关方沟通状态。"},{"path":"skills/user-profile/SKILL.md","name":"user-profile","description":"Captures, updates, and consults the user profile — who they are, their professional context, projects, personal goals, and work preferences. Use when the user wants the system to learn more about them, says 'do you know me?', 'update my profile', 'I want you to know that...', 'I am...', or shares personally relevant information. Also trigger proactively when the user mentions a job change, new client, new personal goal, or change of context.","headings":["Skill: user-profile","What this skill does","When to trigger","Step 1 — Read current profile","Step 2 — Capture new information","Step 3 — Profile structure","Identity","Professional context","Professional goals","Personal context","How to interact","Step 4 — Create client contexts","Step 5 — Confirm","Privacy"],"name_hint":"user · profile","description_zh":"采集、更新和查询用户档案，记录职业背景、项目、个人目标及工作偏好；用于补充个人信息或反映换工作、新客户、目标及情境变化。"},{"path":"skills/weekly-review/SKILL.md","name":"weekly-review","description":"Weekly review that consolidates tasks, unlogged meetings, at-risk contexts, and a preview of next week. Use ALWAYS when the user says 'weekly review', 'friday review', 'how was the week', 'close the week', 'week summary', or similar. Scans all task files in the vault, identifies what was completed, what is at risk, contexts without recent contact, and meetings without a logged note, then generates and saves the review.","headings":["Skill: weekly-review","What this skill delivers","Step 1 — Define the period","Step 2 — Scan all tasks","Step 3 — Housekeeping","Step 4 — Check meetings from the week","Step 5 — Check touchpoints","Step 6 — Preview next week","Step 7 — Generate and save the review","Weekly Review — week of MM/DD to MM/DD","✅ Completed this week","🔴 Overdue (urgent action needed)","⚠️ At risk (next 3 business days)","👥 No recent contact (>14 days)","📋 Meetings this week without a note","📅 Next week","🔁 Housekeeping"],"name_hint":"weekly · 评审","description_zh":"扫描知识库任务与会议记录，汇总本周完成事项、风险、长期未联系的上下文和未归档会议，并生成保存周回顾及下周预览。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Mind++ for Claude","Never used this before? Start here.","Why Mind++?","Quickstart in 5 minutes","1. Install the three tools","2. Choose where your vault will live","3. Install the Mind++ plugin","4. Point Claude to your vault folder","5. Run the setup","6. Start using it","What's inside the plugin","13 skills","68 agents","Scheduled tasks","How your vault gets organized","Privacy","Frequently asked questions","Credits","Contributing","License"]},{"path":"docs/README.md","headings":["Mind++ for Claude","Never used this befor